  "structure": {
    "block_count": 56,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Cute, Quirky, and Easy to Say: 19 Adorable Welsh Baby Girl Names",
        "text_sha256": "1ef85c948e38c2817032d1a4ecf2b171426840552d9dac748acbf3d19b572f2a",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "welsh baby girl names",
        "text_sha256": "31b297a878f7818ad9195d813a0a0d81a842e3211a704b1d8b40d0b184c3dce4",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Popular in Wales, these sweet names are still under-the-radar in the U.S. Take some inspiration for your newest arrival from among these fresh Welsh baby girl names.",
        "text_sha256": "c296d1ca10b594f79745bfa1807df9cb84b2f0185e5ed6bf7d556924c02d8827",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Often underrated and overlooked — especially in the U.S. — Welsh baby girl names are some of the cutest around. Not only do many of them end with the oh-so-popular \"-i,\" they're typically short, sweet, and easy to pronounce.",
        "text_sha256": "84453e08bec2bfc77dca0146d9b950bc03b1ae7b558093a34db4eb7f97d05766",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As with Welsh baby boy names , even if you choose a longer name, there's likely to be a built-in nickname (or two) which will give your daughter options as she grows up.",
        "text_sha256": "1a04cad47ad0570907f0b86435029fd0cf70bd9d79114cbe5294c92e01026ece",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have a read through the following Welsh baby girl names, and remember that whichever one you choose, it'll sound fresh and feminine — and probably come with a super sweet meaning too!",
        "text_sha256": "2a851f415dc81bfd6fd1ddd8a6659933e66c91bfa256eec54aa5597f7dac4d97",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Want to keep searching for the perfect baby name? Check out all the fun options in the What to Expect app .",
        "text_sha256": "08e0a0c0296eca59477a8136935ff91d2ffa798750bf756536b6bc5e6b446656",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Alys. The Welsh twist on Alice, Alys (which you can also spell with an \"i\" — Alis) is simple but unique.",
        "text_sha256": "45bd56e0700bda23f30fd751b5e8a6b587d4bab1c3d87d89a57fd934553116b7",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Bethan. You guessed it: Bethan is an alternative to Bethany, minus the \"-y\" ending. Easy to spell and intuitive to pronounce, your daughter will thank you for giving her such a bold but pretty name.",
        "text_sha256": "d64cd18ffaaf30546057ceaf9c7930c1b9ac601de5927045ef2510e472a8f32d",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cariad. The Welsh-language equivalent of \"sweetheart\" or \"darling\" as a term of endearment, Cariad is a strong name which offers a nice twist on the more common Carrie.",
        "text_sha256": "44a049028ef2b02fcb5f356bddf9724b1852645bdcb6aea75d8778c412089d8c",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Carys. From the Welsh \"to love\" — caru — Carys is an adorable name that means, unsurprisingly, \"beloved.\" (It's also the name of Welsh actress Catherine Zeta-Jones' daughter.) Cerys is an equally lovely alternative spelling.",
        "text_sha256": "595027de9d50a92895df3e0201a0e4f9270aaa685cf90c3b7ae66431e93340e0",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Catrin. Catrin is bold and a touch sophisticated, while still leaving room for softer, more traditional nicknames like Cat and Kitty.",
        "text_sha256": "96bae4f068b4d8e0b5719c3f5361f28822d787458f71df54643dbb660e3d8bbc",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Eira. Eira is the Welsh word for \"snow\" — and while it's one of the more uncommon names on the list, it's also incredibly delicate and an unusual alternative to current favorites like Emma and Ava.",
        "text_sha256": "9ade0d6e9b1da389f18fac37b598f26203726aa63642f236b0b8cd85916d42eb",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Eirlys. Eirlys, taken from the Welsh word for \"snowdrop\" and pronounced ire-liss, sounds just as delicate — and, thanks to the close-sounding iris, recalls the trend towards floral baby girl names.",
        "text_sha256": "b7b3d6e1d502b7a583723a061335080795a6ecc10309228ad0c4d99b4e282da6",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Elen. Helen becomes Elen (or Elin) in Welsh, a chipper name originally derived from Greek meaning \"sunshine\" or \"light.\" Elen was also the name of a Welsh saint.",
        "text_sha256": "e5d777fbe19b7eb89e395a82f170830b4b9cc79ad0c998320535beade7ad68fa",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Enfys. Technically unisex but used more often for girls, Enfys (pronounced en-viss) means \"rainbow\" — making it the perfect name for parents expecting again after a loss.",
        "text_sha256": "3b5bb85e8f0aac6039a8f566b3dd256de26b7a9049dd58d66a9935ca33acf01f",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ffion. Although the double \"ff\" might look confusing, it's pronounced like a single \"f.\" Ffion is the Welsh version of an equally charming Gaelic name: Fiona.",
        "text_sha256": "76fcbae5bfeca4c70d5c6d3d61c9e775dead5b4322eca759dde99e741abb09b1",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Gwen. Very popular in the 20th century, Gwen — as in Gwen Stefani — will have people going b-a-n-a-n-a-s over it again soon! Gwen is also a shortened version of Gwendolyn and related to the French name Guinevere.",
        "text_sha256": "27b1b29c3fe0974bbd38c8aca9694fc455128d960d3aee78a05e7465748113c3",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Lowri. If you like the names Laura and Lauren, Lowri is a quirkier Welsh alternative. Like those more popular variants, it also means \"laurel.\"",
        "text_sha256": "2233d198b990a10befc6d004998aa7508f5ce6f31830ca93da97508d2e792256",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Mari. If you want a classic-sounding name that will stand the test of time, consider Mari — which is also common in Scandinavia and Eastern Europe.",
        "text_sha256": "01d80e781668380de9805c70a724c3d4d284b1f964262e3ee634270594ad0217",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Meleri. A relatively unusual name with ancient roots but a modern sound, Meleri was a Welsh saint. You can shorten to Eleri and even Leri.",
        "text_sha256": "0b5d656ed428baf4cbb031b3dd85d5e30883faba8448f74c4f390b90cf63656e",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Nia. Both Welsh and Swahili in origin, Nia offers a bold twist on the popular baby girl name Mia. Purposeful and strong, Nia also means \"light\" and is the Welsh form of Niamh, a common Irish name.",
        "text_sha256": "f57d676df942506543743e7f6e37b81791e389a7510ea9771912a5d6c4e48a66",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Olwen. One of the more unique \"-wen\" names, Olwen has strong Lord of the Rings vibes without being a direct copy of the half-elven Arwen.",
        "text_sha256": "d0fa282a83a88415d777c309d8fba1840c9ef013a71008b322cdc518d4aa5835",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Rhiannon. Rhiannon is a very popular girls name in Wales but relatively uncommon elsewhere. Lovely-sounding and lyrical, it can also be shortened to Rhian or Rhi.",
        "text_sha256": "9fd699de5fa43a7d555abe21b786357dd9f33de4436d1b5a8cc34bf4eaf296dc",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Seren. Who doesn't want their little lady to shine bright? Seren, the Welsh word for \"star,\" is a sophisticated-sounding girl's name that toes the line between popular and under-the-radar.",
        "text_sha256": "6b0bcdb39cf8a07eac4ee3b8807aa0ee7846c820b8b2a2093f7a604aec19f329",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Tegan. Almost unisex in sound, Tegan means \"beloved\" or \"favorite\" — perfect if you're planning on having just one child! You can also spell it the Irish way: Teagan.",
        "text_sha256": "2372b7e994185d4390b922bc91dfa39a4a04afbc5b815de41e93f1b69d6b5e75",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Lauren Cocking is a Yorkshire-born, Mexico City-based writer, book reviewer and translator. She’s currently at work on her first literary translation and studying Welsh. Cocking has bylines at BBC Travel , CNN, Lonely Planet, National Geographic, OZY, LitHub, Teen Vogue, Al Jazeera and more . She writes about Latin American literature on her blog .",
        "text_sha256": "9e9f9f2675d6651578000bec5391b6759923cfec7dda02656b4b3bb2cd3b98fd",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Updates history",
        "text_sha256": "8ce5f24a37ab68e01743f0cb3f0234dd767a31a441e3e3be35047619722ffec6",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "September 26, 2025",
        "text_sha256": "0c82451909bb66f5b4fcc995e9f672040705e4c6ab3b334e293c10e5e6e3f3c0",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
